    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for the create-owner flow so the flag appears (as `true`/`false`) in the owner response.\n\n**Semantics:** `bulkSignupWarning` is `true` when **more than 80 *other* owners** already share this owner's effective (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2014 i.e. more than 80 owners had already been created that day before this one \u2014 otherwise `false`. This mirrors the accumulation path of the existing daily-limit rule (`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`), excluding the owner itself by id so the boundary is correct (81st same-day owner \u2192 `false`, 82nd \u2192 `true`).\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` (boolean, read-only) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct mapping pick it up automatically at build.\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field with getter/setter (derived, not persisted).\n3. **`AssignBulkSignupWarning`** (new function) \u2014 counts owners sharing the registration date (excluding self) via `OwnerRepository` and sets the flag with a threshold of `> 80`.\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the step after `save`, before `respond` (under `transaction` governance).\n5. **`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 inserted the step after `load`, before `respond` (under `readonly-transaction`), so reads derive the flag consistently \u2014 which is exactly what the `Cp22Tests` acceptance test verifies (creates one owner, then `GET`s it and asserts `bulkSignupWarning == false`).\n\nThe `Cp22Tests` (bulk-warning), `Cp21Tests` (daily-limit, verifying no regression on the shared accumulation path), and the full 33-test suite all pass.",
